  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 1208 AM MST Sat Nov 7 2026\n\nThe long term is forecast to start with an upper trough swinging \nthrough the Plains and Eastern United States. For now, it looks like \nthe trough will swing late enough that there won't be much impact on \nTuesday. Highs are forecast to reach the 60s again underneath mostly \nsunny skies and light winds around 10 mph.\n\nWednesday through Friday are forecast to be under the influence of \nthe upper trough as a reinforcing wave moves in from the Great Lakes \naround Thursday. High temperatures are forecast to still be in the \n60s, though maybe a bit cooler compared to Tuesday. If the trough \naxis digs farther west into the area (30% chances), then highs \nwould likely be a bit cooler in the 50s. We could also see more \ncloud cover with higher level moisture moving through. \nOtherwise, winds should be light with a weak pressure gradient \nin place and no precipitation with dry low and mid levels \nforecast.\n\nFriday and into Saturday, upper level ridging is forecast to push in \nfrom the west and  set up over the region. While likely either \nslightly split and/or broad, we should see temperatures warm a bit \nmore that the prior days. For now, lows 60s is forecast, but highs \nnear 70 would be possible if the cold air mass pushes out early \nFriday. Winds should remain light and no precipitation is\nforecast.",
